# text = I always looked on her as to be my wife -- some time ; and she has often and often spoken of you as the kindest lady that ever was ; and though the plain truth is , I would not like to be troubled with lodgers of the common run , yet if , ma'am , you'd honour us by living with us , I'm sure Martha would do her best to make you comfortable ; and I'd keep out of your way as much as I could , which I reckon would be the best kindness such an awkward chap as me could do Don't let any thought of me hurry you into marriage : pray don't .
